# deml — Cursor rules (design system LOCKED)

You are working in the DEML control-plane repo. Visual design is owned by **deml-ui**.
The **new-from-the-start / atelier** look is **mandatory** for all future product UI.

## Design system (required)

- **SoT:** `deml-ui` (sibling repo / `github:dataengineeringformachinelearning/deml-ui#main`).
- **Look:** new-from-the-start / atelier — 8px grid, dual `data-theme`, bold display + letterspaced marks, equal tile distribution, fixed `--chart-aspect` (2.4), WCAG 2.0 AA.
- **Docs:** `THEME.md` (locked SoT), `docs/DEML_UI.md`, `AGENTS.md` (deml-ui Uniformity Law).
- **Storybook:** https://ui.deml.app

## Do

- Compose product pages with `app-banner`, `app-page-section`, `app-section-header`, `app-tile-board`, `app-dashboard-grid`, `app-card-grid`, `app-stat-card`, `app-chart-card`, `app-area-chart`, `app-bar-chart`.
- Keep Angular wrappers under `src/app/components` with `ViewEncapsulation.None` and **no** component CSS for design-system chrome (`styleUrl` / `styleUrls` / inline `styles` forbidden on DS wrappers).
- Use deml-ui CSS variables only (`--color-*`, `--space-*`, `--tile-*`, `--chart-*`).
- Keep equal outer spacing (8px multiples) and identical card/bento heights via `--tile-row-unit` + `--tile-gap`.
- Preserve chart aspect (`--chart-aspect`); never squash or stretch plots.
- Prefer WCAG 2.0 AA: focus-visible, contrast, ≥44px hit targets, reduced motion.
- Dual theme via `data-theme="light"|"dark"` on `<html>`.

## Do not

- Use or restore **Viking-UI** (`packages/viking-ui`, `@dataengineeringformachinelearning/viking-ui`, `viking-*`, `--viking-*`, void-black / electric `#2176ff` suite chrome).
- Add Material, Bootstrap, Tailwind utility styling, or a parallel local design system.
- Hand-edit `backend/static/deml-ui.css` — sync from deml-ui via `scripts/sync_deml_ui_static.sh`.
- Put product UI back under `frontend/` (that folder is a Vercel rootDirectory shim only).
- Invent one-off spacing, free-resize charts, or app-owned DS tokens.

## When changing visuals

1. Edit deml-ui `components/` + `styles/tokens.css` / `styles/base.css`.
2. `npm run build` in deml-ui (dist is consumed by github installs).
3. Bump deml’s `deml-ui` dependency / lockfile.
4. Sync Django static if templates need the new CSS.

**Locked:** The new style is mandatory for all future work — see `THEME.md`.
